      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SQUAD GOAL (5) has the most persuasive current profile after breaking through at Northam as favourite, beating Arrestedevelopment by a length and a half. She's gone to another level since stepping up to the mile and she doesn't look like stopping just yet. Form out of the maiden has stood up and she can win again. GILDED REIGN (6) has to rebound from a fifth at this track, but the quick back-up is a positive and Lucy Fiore riding is a big tick. Drawn nicely and can bounce back to form in what looks a suitable race. PINCER MOVEMENT (4) resumes after five months. He has trialled at Lark Hill and gets Pike back aboard, so his lightly raced profile keeps him very relevant if forward enough. POINT ROCKS (3) was runner-up here last week after covering ground. That effort stacks up in this field and he can't be left out from a good draw. VANCOUVER STORM (8) can bounce back to form.",
